  "result": "Model makers do use reinforcement learning (RL) to train the models that agents run on. But you should not train your own model for the makerspace assistant.\n\n**Why not:**\n- Your mission puts training and the math inside models out of scope.\n- Training needs many example runs, a reward signal, and GPUs. Your budget is small.\n- A hosted model already calls tools well. Most tool-call errors come from the setup around it.\n\n**What to do instead:**\n1. Write clear tool descriptions. Say what each tool does, when to use it, and what the inputs mean.\n2. Return clear errors, so the model can retry.\n3. Log failed calls. Fix the description that caused each failure.\n\n**PPO in one idea:** the model tries actions and gets a reward. PPO raises the chance of actions with high reward. It also limits each update to a small step, so the model does not change too much at once.\n\nThink of a student learning a 3D printer. They try a setting and see the result. They change a little each time, not everything at once.\n\nI can teach tool descriptions in a lesson. That is the best use of your time before the design review.\n\nSay a tool called `book_machine` fails often. What would you change first?",
